# Paths only the repo owner may change.
#
# CODEOWNERS on its own only *requests* review — it blocks nothing unless
# branch protection requires code-owner approval, which this repo does not
# set. The enforcement is .github/workflows/owner-only.yml, which closes a
# non-owner PR touching any path below. This file is the human-readable
# statement of the same list, and tests/test_pr_eval_bot.py asserts the two
# never drift apart.
#
# Why these and not others: everything here either grades a PR, decides what
# "measured" means, or configures how the engine is built. A contributor PR
# editing one of them is asking to be judged by rules it wrote itself.
# braid/reference/ and tests/ are deliberately NOT here — they are pinned
# during the eval and already cap a verdict at eval:tainted, which the
# outcome policy closes on its own.

# The grader, its cron wrapper, and the scorer shipped into the TEE
/scripts/pr_eval_bot.py    @plind-junior
/scripts/pr_eval_cron.sh   @plind-junior
/scripts/eval_scorer.py    @plind-junior

# CI, the gates, and the PR template that carries the 5090 attestation box
/.github/                  @plind-junior

# How the engine is built, and the contract contributors are held to
/Makefile                  @plind-junior
/pyproject.toml            @plind-junior
/CONTRIBUTING.md           @plind-junior

# The benchmark harness a verdict is read from
/braid/bench/              @plind-junior
